==Strategy==
Ururun Wolf appears once again, this time with the assistance of Super Cosmic Cyclone, alongside Mr. Angels and Miz Devils. Even though the Cyclone has relatively low damage, it can still push forward thanks to its warp and the extra support.
You can either take it down before advancing towards Ururun or use Super Cosmic Cyclone and the smaller peons as stepping stones for [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] units to take her down.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] - Decently durable Warp Immune meatshield against Super Cosmic Cyclone.
*[[Green Shell Cat]] - Tanky throwaway unit, capable of holding back the enemies and supporting your meatshield line.
*[[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Bakery Cat]] - His Curse allows for the usage of non-Warp Immune meatshields, such as [[Manic Eraser Cat]] and, if you have progressed enough at [[Behemoth Culling]], [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]]. True form makes it easier to curse Super Cosmic Cyclone by increasing its standing range and giving Area Attack, removing the possibility of his attack being wasted on a peon. Just make sure the Cyclone isn't too close to Ururun Wolf.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] - Can clear smaller peons and produce Waves capable of damaging Ururun. Unlocking its True Form makes usage easier.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs Cat]] - Mid-ranged Wave attacker, capable of hitting all enemies on the stage by attacking the frontline.
*[[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] - A Cat specifically made to snipe backliners by using enemies as stepping stones. In this case, it can attack Ururun from the Cyclone. Due to being outranged by it and lacking Warp Immunity, he requires Bakery Cat or another Curse unit to work, yet won't be able to stack.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - Can freeze Super Cosmic Cyclone with the help of Weaken and Curse units or his Immune to Warp Talent.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] - if true formed, can completely nullify Super Cosmic's attacks & allow your Seafarers to easily get hits in. He will inevitably die due to Ururun's pushing, but can serve to take care of the cyclone for a while, especially if it is near your base. Just make sure to protect him well, as he is very fragile.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]] - She has Massive Damage against Aliens while outranging Ururun Wolf, having great damage to combat her, and thanks to LD, she can use the Cyclone to attack Ururun.
*[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] - Similar case to Aphrodite, but with Massive Damage against Traitless, allowing him to quickly kill Ururun Wolf. Due to his lower range (340<415), you must use Super Cosmic Cyclone as a stepping stone to make full usage of him.
*[[Voli (Uber Rare Cat)|Gigavolta]] - Can safely freeze the Super Cosmic Cyclone from afar, while having extra resistance and Warp Immunity in case it manages to reach him.
*[[Mekako Saionji (Uber Rare Cat)|Mission Control Mekako]] - She can deal very high damage to the Super Cosmic Cyclone while halting it's movement with guaranteed Slow and also possibly Weaken/Knockback it if you invested in those Talents.
*[[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]] - Similar case to Mekako, but with higher damage at the cost of not inflicting debuffs and only targeting the Cyclone (and also Ururun if their Target Traitless Ultra Talent has been unlocked).

